	Hi there,

		I think that the game balance is really well done, for
it gives a challenge to the novice player, BUT NOT IMPOSSIBLE. If
there are things that a novice wants, then there are a few ways of
generating them. It should be up to the egotistical to deny themselves
some of the features, choose difficult classes, etc. but do not force
these hardships upon the beginner, who will give up with frustration.
    Perhaps have a scoreboard for those who have ascended, giving a
line or two for them to comment upon their game, and if the viewer of
the board wishes to see the gamers inventory upon completion, then
they may. (Just to see if they REALLY did finish with no armour.)
    Please do not end up adding Ancient Multi-Hued Dragons in (a-la
Moria) which breathe instant-death from round a corner, as
ultra-powerful monsters will wreck the balance. (Orcs with wands of
death? Well, I can run around with a wand of death, so that's fair.)

	Steve T.

